.TH "FLOX\-AUTH" "1" "" "" "Flox User Manuals"
.SH NAME
flox\-auth \- FloxHub authentication commands
.SH SYNOPSIS
.IP
.EX
flox [<general\-options>] auth
     (login | logout | status | token)
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
Authenticate with FloxHub so that you can push and pull environments.
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS \f[CR]login\f[R]
Logs in to FloxHub.
.PP
Required to interact with environments on FloxHub via
\f[CR]flox push\f[R], \f[CR]flox pull\f[R], and
\f[CR]flox activate \-r\f[R].
Authenticating also automatically trusts your personal environments.
.PP
Prompts you to enter a one\-time code at a specified URL.
If called interactively it can open the browser for you if you press
\f[CR]<enter>\f[R].
.PP
See also: \f[B]\f[CB]flox\-push(1)\f[B]\f[R],
\f[B]\f[CB]flox\-pull(1)\f[B]\f[R],
\f[B]\f[CB]flox\-activate(1)\f[B]\f[R]
.SS \f[CR]logout\f[R]
Logs out from FloxHub.
.SS \f[CR]status\f[R]
Print your current login status.
.SS \f[CR]token\f[R]
Print the current authentication token to stdout.
